; ==========================================================================
; STELLAR MAZE  -  VM1: builds the maze, hands it over   (loads at $4000)
; ==========================================================================
; Load BOTH programs - Maze-VM1.lst at $4000 and Maze-VM2.lst at $5000 - then
; cold-boot and press a key. VM1 carves a random 25 x 10 maze on screen (a
; depth-first backtracker, multitasking OFF so it has the whole CPU). Then it
; copies the grid into VM2's memory with $DC COPYBVMXVMY and triggers VM2 by
; writing 1 into VM2's RB with $D3 COPYVXY. VM2 solves it right-hand-on-the-wall:
; 'o' is the path, '.' the dead ends it backed out of.
;
; VT100: cursor addressing and reverse video (the walls) only.
;
; VERIFICATION (Firmware-Math/maze_verify.py, V0061.33, two-VM cold boot): three mazes (the key pressed at three different moments) each read back off the screen as a PERFECT 25 x 10 maze equal to VM1's grid; VM2's copy has identical walls (all 1,196 bytes moved by $DC); the 'o' left on screen is exactly the start-to-exit path, '.' only off it, and the step and path counts match a Python right-hand walk. About 15.6 million 1802 instructions (~1.5 min at 3 MHz) + ~12 KB of output (~13 s at 9600 baud).
; NOT YET RUN ON HARDWARE.
;
; 155 STELLAR commands.
;
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------
; DISASSEMBLY  -  commented out; the loader skips it
; --------------------------------------------------------------------------

; D 4000 CD             START
; D 4001 11 0F 00 0A    LOADXI R15 000A
; D 4005 11 0C 00 34    LOADXI R12 0034                    The grid stride
; D 4009 11 0A 00 02    LOADXI R10 0002
; D 400D D0 11          SHAREVM on, read-only              VM2 may read us (the $DC source)
; WAIT2:
; D 400F D1 22          TESTVM 2 RW                        Has VM2 opened itself read/write yet?
; D 4011 A1 00 0F       IFFALSEI WAIT2                     Not yet - it needs one turn first
; D 4014 11 0E 06 00    LOADXI R14 0600
; D 4018 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 401A 11 0E 06 44    LOADXI R14 0644
; D 401E C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; SEED:
; D 4020 C3             RAND                               Spin the generator until a key comes - every maze differs
; D 4021 CC             SERST
; D 4022 A1 00 20       IFFALSEI SEED
; D 4025 CB             SERIN                              and throw the key away
; D 4026 C7 00          SETMULTI 00                        Multitasking OFF: VM2 is only waiting
; D 4028 11 0E 06 72    LOADXI R14 0672
; D 402C C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 402E 11 0E 06 B4    LOADXI R14 06B4
; D 4032 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       Reverse video: a space is a wall block
; D 4034 11 0D 00 03    LOADXI R13 0003
; D 4038 11 03 00 15    LOADXI R3 0015
; BLK:
; D 403C 11 0E 00 0F    LOADXI R14 000F
; D 4040 BD 01 93       CALL POSXY
; D 4043 11 0E 07 C0    LOADXI R14 07C0
; D 4047 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14                       51 blocks
; D 4049 42 0D          INCX R13
; D 404B 43 03          DECX R3
; D 404D 8C 03          TESTXZ R3
; D 404F A1 00 3C       IFFALSEI BLK
; D 4052 11 0E 06 B9    LOADXI R14 06B9
; D 4056 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4058 11 07 00 20    LOADXI R7 0020                     R7 = the carving character, a normal-video space
; D 405C 11 0B 00 35    LOADXI R11 0035
; D 4060 BD 01 7B       CALL DRAW                          The way in (screen only)
; D 4063 11 0B 04 75    LOADXI R11 0475
; D 4067 BD 01 7B       CALL DRAW                          The way out
; D 406A 11 06 00 69    LOADXI R6 0069
; D 406E 10 00 20       LOADAI 0020
; D 4071 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800                   Carve the first cell
; D 4075 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 4078 BD 01 7B       CALL DRAW
; D 407B 11 01 0D 00    LOADXI R1 0D00                     R1 = stack pointer
; D 407F 3A 02 61       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R1)                push it
; D 4082 52 01 00 02    ADDXI R1 0002
; LOOP:
; D 4086 86 01 0D 00    TESTXI R1 0D00
; D 408A A0 01 4E       IFTRUEI BUILT                      Stack empty: every cell visited
; D 408D 23 00 18       COPYXY R1 -> R8
; D 4090 53 08 00 02    SUBXI R8 0002
; D 4094 39 02 82       COPYMXY M(R8) -> R2                R2 = current cell
; D 4097 11 05 00 00    LOADXI R5 0000                     R5 = unvisited neighbours found
; D 409B 11 09 0F 00    LOADXI R9 0F00
; D 409F 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40A2 52 06 00 02    ADDXI R6 0002                      right
; D 40A6 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 40AA 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 40AD A1 00 B9       IFFALSEI NB0
; D 40B0 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 40B3 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 40B7 42 05          INCX R5
; NB0:
; D 40B9 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40BC 53 06 00 02    SUBXI R6 0002                      left
; D 40C0 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 40C4 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 40C7 A1 00 D3       IFFALSEI NB1
; D 40CA 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 40CD 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 40D1 42 05          INCX R5
; NB1:
; D 40D3 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40D6 52 06 00 68    ADDXI R6 0068                      down
; D 40DA 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 40DE 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 40E1 A1 00 ED       IFFALSEI NB2
; D 40E4 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 40E7 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 40EB 42 05          INCX R5
; NB2:
; D 40ED 23 00 26       COPYXY R2 -> R6
; D 40F0 53 06 00 68    SUBXI R6 0068                      up
; D 40F4 2E 06 08 00    READIDX R6 0800
; D 40F8 81 00 23       TESTAI 0023                        '#' = unvisited ('X' = off the edge)
; D 40FB A1 01 07       IFFALSEI NB3
; D 40FE 3A 02 69       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R9)                a candidate
; D 4101 52 09 00 02    ADDXI R9 0002
; D 4105 42 05          INCX R5
; NB3:
; D 4107 8C 05          TESTXZ R5
; D 4109 A1 01 13       IFFALSEI PICK
; D 410C 53 01 00 02    SUBXI R1 0002                      Dead end: pop
; D 4110 B0 00 86       GAL LOOP
; PICK:
; D 4113 C3             RAND                               A random one of them
; D 4114 21 06          COPYAX Acc -> R6
; D 4116 4D 65          DIVXY R6 / R5
; D 4118 27             COPYREMA
; D 4119 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8
; D 411B 50 88 08       ADDXYZ R8 + R8 -> R8               x2: a word each
; D 411E 52 08 0F 00    ADDXI R8 0F00
; D 4122 39 02 86       COPYMXY M(R8) -> R6                R6 = the chosen cell
; D 4125 50 26 08       ADDXYZ R2 + R6 -> R8
; D 4128 4D 8A          DIVXY R8 / R10
; D 412A 25             COPYMAA
; D 412B 21 08          COPYAX Acc -> R8                   R8 = the wall between = (cur + next) / 2
; D 412D 10 00 20       LOADAI 0020
; D 4130 2F 08 08 00    WRITEIDX R8 0800                   knock it down
; D 4134 2F 06 08 00    WRITEIDX R6 0800                   and visit the cell
; D 4138 23 00 8B       COPYXY R8 -> R11
; D 413B BD 01 7B       CALL DRAW
; D 413E 23 00 6B       COPYXY R6 -> R11
; D 4141 BD 01 7B       CALL DRAW
; D 4144 3A 02 61       COPYXMY R6 -> M(R1)                push it
; D 4147 52 01 00 02    ADDXI R1 0002
; D 414B B0 00 86       GAL LOOP
; BUILT:
; D 414E 11 03 08 00    LOADXI R3 0800                     The grid is at the same place in both VMs
; D 4152 11 06 00 05    LOADXI R6 0005
; COPY:
; D 4156 D3 21 33       COPYVXY save R3 -> VM2 R3          VM2's R3 = the same address, in VM2
; D 4159 DC 13 23 F0    COPYBVMXVMY VM1 R3 -> VM2 R3 F0    240 bytes, VM1 to VM2
; D 415D 52 03 00 F0    ADDXI R3 00F0
; D 4161 43 06          DECX R6
; D 4163 8C 06          TESTXZ R6
; D 4165 A1 01 56       IFFALSEI COPY
; D 4168 11 0B 00 01    LOADXI R11 0001
; D 416C D3 21 BB       COPYVXY save RB -> VM2 RB          The trigger: VM2 is waiting for RB = 1
; D 416F 11 0E 06 BE    LOADXI R14 06BE
; D 4173 C1 0E          PRINTSTR R14
; D 4175 C7 01          SETMULTI 01                        Multitasking back ON - VM2 takes over
; D 4177 00             HALT                               VM1 is done
; D 4178 F0 00 00       BREAK
; DRAW:
; D 417B 4D BC          DIVXY R11 / R12                    row + 1, column
; D 417D 25             COPYMAA
; D 417E 21 0D          COPYAX Acc -> R13
; D 4180 52 0D 00 02    ADDXI R13 0002
; D 4184 27             COPYREMA
; D 4185 21 0E          COPYAX Acc -> R14
; D 4187 52 0E 00 0F    ADDXI R14 000F
; D 418B BD 01 93       CALL POSXY
; D 418E 22 07          COPYXA R7 -> Acc
; D 4190 C9             SEROUT
; D 4191 BE 00          RETURN
; POSXY:
; D 4193 CA 1B          SEROUTI 1B
; D 4195 CA 5B          SEROUTI 5B '['
; D 4197 4D DF          DIVXY R13 / R15
; D 4199 25             COPYMAA
; D 419A 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 419D C9             SEROUT
; D 419E 27             COPYREMA
; D 419F 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41A2 C9             SEROUT
; D 41A3 CA 3B          SEROUTI 3B ';'
; D 41A5 4D EF          DIVXY R14 / R15
; D 41A7 25             COPYMAA
; D 41A8 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41AB C9             SEROUT
; D 41AC 27             COPYREMA
; D 41AD 4E 00 30       ADDAI 0030
; D 41B0 C9             SEROUT
; D 41B1 CA 48          SEROUTI 48 'H'
; D 41B3 BE 00          RETURN

